{"context":"The Code Discovery and Context indexer uses `filepath.Walk` (or equivalent) which follows symlinks. When encountering a symlinked directory (e.g., Flutter's `.plugin_symlinks`), the current logic fails with `is a directory`. We need a deterministic strategy to handle symlinks during index generation without infinite cycles.","decision":"Safely follow symlinks during indexing. The indexer will maintain a path cache (`os.Lstat` / inode set) to detect and skip cycles. A `--follow-symlinks` flag (default true) will be exposed for opt-out.","consequences":"- Indexer accurately processes code within plugin boundaries.\n- Requires cycle detection to prevent infinite recursion.\n- New CLI flag `-s, --follow-symlinks=true|false` added.","alternativesConsidered":"- **Skip symlinks**: Simple, avoids cycles, but skips valid code (e.g., Flutter plugins).\n- **Error on symlinks**: Current bug behavior, blocks usage."}